sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Student
    participant Monaco as Monaco Editor Component
    participant API as Axios REST Service
    participant Router as Express Problem Router
    participant Service as Submission Controller
    participant ASTGuard as AST Lexical Guard
    participant Sandbox as Local Sandbox Runner (VM / Python)
    participant Judge0 as Judge0 Cloud API (Fallback)
    participant DB as MongoDB Atlas (submissions, users)

    Student->>Monaco: Types code solution & clicks "Submit Solution"
    Monaco->>API: POST /api/problems/:slug/submit {code, language}
    API->>Router: Authenticated HTTP Request (JWT Bearer Token)
    Router->>Service: handleCodeSubmission(problemSlug, code, language, user)
    Service->>DB: Fetch Problem Document (Sample & Hidden Test Cases)
    DB-->>Service: Returns Problem Statement & Test Case Array

    Note over Service,ASTGuard: STATIC ANALYSIS & DEFENSE-IN-DEPTH SCAN
    Service->>ASTGuard: inspectCode(code, language)
    ASTGuard->>ASTGuard: Tokenize AST & check forbidden tokens (require, process, import os, eval)

    alt AST Security Violation Detected
        ASTGuard-->>Service: Violation Flagged ("Unauthorized System Access")
        Service-->>Router: 400 Bad Request { error: "Security violation detected" }
        Router-->>API: 400 Error Response
        API-->>Monaco: Render Security Warning Banner
    else AST Security Check Passed
        ASTGuard-->>Service: Code Structure Clean (Pass)

        Note over Service,Sandbox: DUAL-ENGINE TEST CASE EXECUTION
        opt Local Sandbox Execution (Default)
            Service->>Sandbox: execute(code, language, testCases)
            loop For Each Test Case (Sample + Hidden)
                Sandbox->>Sandbox: Instantiate Null-Prototype Isolated Context
                Sandbox->>Sandbox: Execute with 3000ms CPU Timeout & Memory Ceiling
                Sandbox->>Sandbox: Compare Normalized Stdout with Expected Output
            end
            Sandbox-->>Service: Execution Results { status: "Accepted", runtime: 42ms, memory: 14MB }
        end
        opt External Engine Fallback (If Configured)
            Service->>Judge0: POST /submissions/batch {source_code, stdin, expected_output}
            Judge0-->>Service: Batch Results JSON
        end

        Note over Service,DB: RESULT PERSISTENCE & METRIC MUTATION
        Service->>DB: Submissions.create({ userId, problemId, code, status: "Accepted", runtime, memory })
        Service->>DB: Problems.updateOne({ $inc: { totalSubmissions: 1, solvedCount: 1 } })
        Service->>DB: Users.updateOne({ $inc: { problemsSolved: 1 }, $set: { streak: newStreak } })
        DB-->>Service: Database Operations Confirmed
        Service-->>Router: 200 OK { success: true, submissionId, status: "Accepted", passed: 5, total: 5 }
        Router-->>API: 200 OK JSON Payload
        API-->>Monaco: Trigger Results Drawer & Fire Victory Confetti
    end